RULE                              SEVERITY  FIXABLE  DESCRIPTION
heading-increment                 warning   no       Each heading is at most one level deeper than the heading or title before it.
heading-style                     warning   yes      Headings all use the first heading's style: # Title, # Title #, or underlined.
unordered-list-style              warning   yes      Every bullet uses the same marker as the first bullet in the file.
list-indent                       warning   yes      Items in a list start at the same column. Ordered numbers may right-align.
ul-indent                         warning   yes      Outside ordered lists, bullets sit at the margin and indent 2 spaces per level.
no-trailing-spaces                warning   yes      Outside code blocks, lines end in no spaces or tabs, or in exactly 2 of them.
no-hard-tabs                      warning   yes      Lines contain no tab characters, including inside code.
no-reversed-links                 warning   yes      Inline links put the text in brackets and the URL in parentheses: [text](url).
no-multiple-blank-lines           warning   yes      Outside code, no two blank lines follow each other, except after front matter.
line-length                       warning   yes      Lines fit in 80 characters, with exemptions such as lone links and definitions.
commands-show-output              warning   yes      Code blocks that show only commands leave out the $ prompt.
no-missing-space-atx              warning   yes      A space follows the # marks that open a heading at the start of a line.
no-multiple-space-atx             warning   yes      Only one space follows the # marks that open a heading.
no-missing-space-closed-atx       warning   yes      A closed heading at the start of a line has a space inside each run of #.
no-multiple-space-closed-atx      warning   yes      A closed heading has only one space inside each run of #.
heading-blank-lines               warning   yes      Headings have a blank or comment line above and below.
heading-start-left                warning   yes      Headings start at the beginning of their line, list item or blockquote.
no-duplicate-heading              warning   no       No two headings have exactly the same text.
single-h1                         warning   no       A document that starts with a title has no other top-level heading.
no-trailing-punctuation           warning   yes      Headings do not end with a period, comma, semicolon, colon or exclamation mark.
no-multiple-space-blockquote      warning   yes      Outside code and list item text, at most one space follows a blockquote's >.
no-blanks-blockquote              warning   no       No blank line sits between two blockquotes.
ol-prefix                         warning   yes      Ordered list items are numbered 1, 1, 1, or 1, 2, 3, or 0, 1, 2, and so on.
list-marker-space                 warning   yes      One space, or one tab, separates each list marker from the item's text.
blanks-around-fences              warning   yes      Fenced code blocks have a blank or comment line above and below.
blanks-around-lists               warning   yes      Lists outside other lists have a blank or comment line above and below.
no-inline-html                    warning   no       Documents contain no raw HTML elements other than allowed ones.
no-bare-urls                      warning   yes      Outside code and HTML, URLs and email addresses sit in angle brackets or links.
hr-style                          warning   yes      Every horizontal rule is written the same way as the first one, such as ---.
no-emphasis-as-heading            warning   yes      Outside lists and blockquotes, a bold or italic line is not a stand-in heading.
no-space-in-emphasis              warning   yes      Emphasis markers touch the text they wrap, as in **bold**.
no-space-in-code                  warning   yes      Code span text has no spaces around it, except one each side or by a backtick.
no-space-in-links                 warning   yes      Link text has no spaces just inside its brackets.
fenced-code-language              warning   yes      Fenced code blocks name their language after the opening fence.
first-line-heading                warning   no       Comments aside, the file starts with a top-level heading or front matter title.
no-empty-links                    warning   no       Inline links have a destination, and no link points at just #.
required-headings                 warning   no       Headings follow the configured outline in order. No outline is set by default.
proper-names                      warning   yes      Outside URLs, proper names match the configured capitals, none by default.
no-alt-text                       warning   no       Markdown images have alt text, and HTML images have alt or aria-hidden="true".
code-block-style                  warning   no       Code blocks all use the first block's style, fenced or indented.
single-trailing-newline           warning   yes      The file ends with a newline, or a last line of only whitespace, > or comments.
code-fence-style                  warning   yes      Code fences all use the first fence's character, backtick or tilde.
emphasis-style                    warning   yes      All italic text uses one marker, *text* or _text_, except * inside a word.
strong-style                      warning   yes      All bold text uses one marker, **text** or __text__, except ** inside a word.
link-fragments                    warning   no       Links to a #fragment point at a heading or anchor in the same file, or at #top.
reference-links-images            warning   no       Labels in [text][label] and [label][] references are defined, except x.
link-image-reference-definitions  warning   yes      Every reference definition is used and defined once, except [//] comments.
link-image-style                  warning   no       Links and images use only the allowed styles. By default, all are allowed.
table-pipe-style                  warning   no       Table rows use leading and trailing pipes the same way throughout.
table-column-count                warning   no       Every table row has as many cells as the header row.
blanks-around-tables              info      yes      Tables have a blank or comment line above and below.
descriptive-link-text             warning   no       Link text describes its target instead of saying "click here" or "more".
table-column-style                warning   no       Each table follows one style: aligned pipes, one space of padding, or none.
link-destination-style            warning   no       Links in a file, other than #fragment links, are all relative or all absolute.
table-alignment                   warning   yes      Each cell of a table's delimiter row has at least 3 dashes.
